@@ -0,0 +1,67 @@
+# Activities
+
+Account activity records card updates and comments across boards the current user can access.
+
+## `GET /:account_slug/activities.json`
+
+Returns a flat, paginated array of events, newest first. Events with the same timestamp are ordered by ID, descending.
+The endpoint includes the same actions as the HTML activity timeline, except that deprecated `card_collection_changed`
+events are omitted and `card_title_changed` events are included.
+
+| Parameter | Type | Required | Description |
+|-----------|------|----------|-------------|
+| `creator_ids[]` | array of strings | No | Only include events created by these users |
+| `board_ids[]` | array of strings | No | Only include events from these boards |
+
+Multiple IDs within a filter match any of those IDs. When both filters are supplied, events must match both.
+Filters never grant access to otherwise inaccessible activity. If no accessible events match, the response is `[]`.
+
+Follow the `Link` header's `rel="next"` URL to fetch subsequent pages, as described in the
+[pagination guide](../README.md#pagination). Next-page links preserve the filters.
+
+__Example request:__
+
+```bash
+curl --get \
+  -H "Authorization: Bearer put-your-access-token-here" \
+  --data-urlencode "creator_ids[]=03f5v9zjw7pz8717a4no1h8a7" \
+  --data-urlencode "board_ids[]=03f5v9zjv1gh36b3n8v2wxyz1" \
+  http://app.fizzy.localhost:3006/897362094/activities.json
+```
+
+__Response fields:__
+
+Each event contains:
+
+| Field | Type | Description |
+|-------|------|-------------|
+| `id` | string | Event ID |
+| `action` | string | Event action, listed below |
+| `created_at` | string | Event timestamp in UTC, in ISO 8601 format |
+| `description` | string | The event's plain-text description, generated for the current user |
+| `particulars` | object | Event-specific details, described below |
+| `url` | string | URL that opens the card; comment events also include an anchor that jumps to the comment |
+| `eventable_type` | string | `Card` or `Comment` |
+| `eventable` | object | The standard [card](cards.md) or [comment](comments.md) API representation |
+| `board` | object | The standard [board](boards.md) API representation |
+| `creator` | object | The standard [user](users.md) API representation of the event creator |
+
+### Actions and particulars
+
+| Action | Particulars |
+|--------|-------------|
+| `card_assigned`, `card_unassigned` | `assignee_ids`: array of user IDs affected by the change |
+| `card_board_changed` | `old_board`, `new_board`: board names |
+| `card_title_changed` | `old_title`, `new_title`: card titles |
+| `card_triaged` | `column`: destination column name |
+| `card_published`, `card_closed`, `card_reopened`, `card_postponed`, `card_auto_postponed`, `card_sent_back_to_triage`, `comment_created` | `{}` |
+
+Missing board names, titles, and column names are returned as empty strings, not `null`.
+Particulars are exposed directly in the object, without an additional nested `particulars` key. For example:
+
+```json
+{
+  "old_title": "Original title",
+  "new_title": "Updated title"
+}
+```
diff --git a/test/controllers/activities_controller_test.rb b/test/controllers/activities_controller_test.rb
